{"availability":"available","full":"krishna0605/krishna0605","name":"krishna0605","description":"Explore this public GitHub project.","category":"Other","language":"Python","stars":1,"forks":0,"created":"2024-09-02T09:02:26Z","updated":"2026-10-10T21:48:28Z","branch":"main","homepage":null,"topics":[],"demo":"https://netra-hackathon-console-20260714.vercel.app/","color":"#302e55","ink":"#dbd2ff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-10T23:20:28.784Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-10T23:20:28.784Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-10T23:20:28.784Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-10T23:20:28.784Z","stars":1,"forks":0}],"technologies":["Python"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["I'm a computer science graduate working across software engineering, cybersecurity, and DevSecOps. I spent six months as a cloud and DevOps intern — configuring environments, validating builds and releases, and deploying services across AWS, Azure, and GCP — and that is where the problem I work on now stopped being theoretical. Most of what goes wrong in a deployed system isn't inside any one component. It's in the space between components, and that space usually has no owner.","My work follows from that: understanding how a code change affects the security of the connected components and the environment they run in. Conflicting assumptions, incompatible interfaces, transitive dependencies, permissions, and configuration drift are the failures I find most interesting, because every one of them passes the checks aimed at a single file.","I'm particularly interested in validating open-source contributions — including those written with AI assistance — by examining the changed code alongside the services, dependencies, and configurations it can reach. That means treating the whole path as one system: development, pre-production testing, CI/CD, and the production environment the change eventually lands in."],"features":["NETWORK FORENSICS & EVIDENCE","A case-oriented investigation platform that turns packet captures into structured evidence, explainable detection signals, and reports with a traceable custody history.","Python Django React PostgreSQL","208 commits · ★ 0 Last commit: 18 Aug 2026 · main","Source code &middot; Controlled demo"],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/krishna0605/krishna0605/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"f19ff69596e78a0354f7aaa6cb23a0368e6c4e4320c6f6a5fb8670057e2c7926","extractedAt":"2026-10-10T23:20:28.879Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-10T23:20:28.879Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"I'm a computer science graduate working across software engineering, cybersecurity, and DevSecOps. I spent six months as a cloud and DevOps intern — configuring environments, validating builds and releases, and deploying services across AWS, Azure, and GCP — and that is where the problem I work on now stopped being theoretical. Most of what goes wrong in a deployed system isn't inside any one component. It's in the space between components, and that space usually has no owner.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/krishna0605/krishna0605/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[],"fingerprint":"f19ff69596e78a0354f7aaa6cb23a0368e6c4e4320c6f6a5fb8670057e2c7926","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/krishna0605/krishna0605/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-10T23:20:28.880Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-10-10T21:48:28Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/krishna0605/krishna0605/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-10T23:20:28.883Z","hash":"f19ff69596e78a0354f7aaa6cb23a0368e6c4e4320c6f6a5fb8670057e2c7926","originalBytes":23401,"storedBytes":23401,"truncated":false,"searchTerms":["mdash","middot","what","how","amp","commit","before","code","work","last","same","security","system","engine","environment","scs","aircraft","c++","change","data","inside","krishna0605","one","python","services","simulator","those","where","against","between","cloud","computer","configuration","each","every","